    <!-- PSM_Cmd — Guide -->
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGHdr">Guide — PSM_Cmd command channel</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGIntro">PSM_Cmd is the secure channel the Hub and services use to send commands to the game server (ps_game/ps_login): /nt messages, EXP multipliers, kicks, boss spawns, etc. It is isolated in a dedicated, closed DB, with a signed CLR assembly (no TRUSTWORTHY), wrappers, allowlist and audit.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGFlowH">How a command travels</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGFlowP">Callers (site, task worker, gameplay) NEVER touch dbo.Command directly. They call a wrapper — usp_SendNotice (only /nt) or usp_RunCommand (allowlisted commands) — which runs EXECUTE AS OWNER, validates, executes and writes the audit. So a credential leak grants no power beyond what the wrapper allows.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGTierH">The Tiers (privilege classes)</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGTierIntro">Every command has a Tier; every login has a max Tier. Increasing power:</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGTierSafe">harmless read/broadcast: /nt, /uc, /si, /mem.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGTierPlayer">acts on players: kick by name/ID, protections.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGTierEconomy">touches the economy: EXP x2, enchant/gem rates, boss spawn, item/gold.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGTierService">destructive: /shutdown, /allout, /crashdump. NOT grantable to logins; stay disabled.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGAllowH">«Command allowlist» tab</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGAllowP">The whitelist of what usp_RunCommand accepts. Per command: Enabled (on/off) and Tier. Enabled rows are highlighted in gold. Rule: a command runs only if Enabled. SERVICE and risky economy commands come disabled by default — enable only what you truly need.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGCallersH">«Caller profiles» tab</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGCallersP">Maps SQL login → max allowed Tier. A login can run a command only if: the command is Enabled AND its Tier ≤ the login's max Tier. Otherwise it is denied (return -3).</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGCallersP2">• Ernoweb@ (web site) = PLAYER → can /nt and kick, never economy.&#x0a;• ShaiyaTaskAgent (scheduled-task worker) = ECONOMY → also EXP x2, boss, etc.&#x0a;The less power a login has, the less damage a leak does.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGLogH">DB Log (audit)</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGLogP">Every attempt ends up in GmCommandLog with a result: OK (executed), DENIED (blocked by allowlist/tier), ERROR (execution error). Useful to see who ran what and why it was possibly refused. From DB Log you can filter and purge old records.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGPracticeH">In practice</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGPracticeP">To enable a new economy command for the worker (e.g. /exp2xenable): in Allowlist set Enabled = on and check that ShaiyaTaskAgent has max Tier ≥ ECONOMY in Profiles. Save. Then check DB Log that the command shows OK, not DENIED.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="PsmGGotIt">Got it</s:String>

